# The keys a release of Collectu Core is signed with, in the allowed signers format of ssh-keygen(1).
#
# A Core updates only to a release whose tag carries a valid signature of one of these keys
# (src/utils/signed_releases.py), and it reads this file from the version it already runs - never
# from the one it is about to install. So a release cannot vouch for itself: the first key has to
# reach a Core with an update it already trusts, and a new key only through a release signed with
# an old one. The release workflow refuses to tag with a key that is not listed here.
#
# Only ed25519 keys are accepted. One line per key:
#
#   release@collectu.de namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# Rotating the key: add the new line next to the old one and release with the old key; switch the
# secret RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY to the new key; remove the old line in a release signed with the new
# one. See "Integrity of Updates" in SECURITY.md.
release@collectu.de namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAINDhqLKhlwHQbHOtJ6vG7sNvROBho17KDMMJM8OmJOV4 collectu-core release signing
